                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcbeb00f-15c1-3ab5-8bc4-88c4b12c1dce",
                        "entry_id": "893a5fad-5f5a-3697-b3b0-19e06cd35a6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To use a starting point for translating a series of nucleotides that is off by an amount not divisible by three, resulting in an entirely distinct set of codons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e18ecc75-4ea4-4c9b-8782-169203e3c4ed",
                                "sense_id": "bcbeb00f-15c1-3ab5-8bc4-88c4b12c1dce",
                                "text": "Commonly, there are stimulatory signals in mRNA distinct from the shift site that greatly increase the level of frameshifting at the shift site."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "272de7ae-b2d2-4fd1-b437-9eed057a6d35",
                                "sense_id": "bcbeb00f-15c1-3ab5-8bc4-88c4b12c1dce",
                                "text": "Considering these costs, it seems likely that mechanisms may exist to stop frameshifted translation as soon as possible, depending on the frequency of occurrence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "573cbe31-f9cb-4ae4-95da-25f06340a726",
                                "sense_id": "bcbeb00f-15c1-3ab5-8bc4-88c4b12c1dce",
                                "text": "Ribosomal frameshifting at a particular site can yield two protein products from one coding sequence or one protein product from two overlapping open reading frames."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
